# Skill: open-pr, opening a PR the way this repo expects

This skill shapes *how* a PR is opened, never *whether*. Run it only when {{OWNER}} has asked for a PR in this conversation. It never merges: merging is {{OWNER}}'s call, with green checks (`AGENTS.md` "How we work" step 6).

## Step 1: Preconditions

Stop at the first one that is missing, and tell {{OWNER}} what's missing.

1. **{{OWNER}} asked for a PR.** If not, offer to open one and stop.
2. **Clean tree:** `git status --porcelain` prints nothing. Work that belongs to this change gets committed in the normal flow first; anything else, ask.
3. **Reviewer approval:** the reviewer ({{PERSONA_NAME_REVIEWER}}) returned APPROVE on this HEAD. If code changed after the approval beyond what the review asked for, run the reviewer again.
<!-- kit:if has.checks -->
4. **Checks on this HEAD:** `{{CMD_CHECKS}}` and `{{CMD_HOOK_TESTS}}`. If they haven't run since the last commit, run them now. A failure, or "not run: <reason>", stops the skill.
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !has.checks -->
4. **Checks on this HEAD:** `{{CMD_HOOK_TESTS}}`. If it hasn't run since the last commit, run it now. A failure stops the skill. The project has no typecheck, lint or test command; say so in Notes as "not run: no command".
<!-- kit:end -->
5. **Branch:** `git branch --show-current` matches `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<type>-<slug>`.
   - `<type>` is one of `feat fix docs style refactor perf test build ci chore revert`;
   - `<slug>` is 2 to 5 kebab-case words.
   On `main` or a mismatch, propose `git branch -m <new name>` to {{OWNER}} and stop.
6. **Base:** run `git fetch origin main`. If `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main HEAD` fails, the branch is behind: propose a rebase to {{OWNER}}, don't rebase on your own. For a stacked PR the base is the branch below; use it wherever `main` appears below.
<!-- kit:if has.container -->
7. **Parity** (not a blocker): if the diff touches the image or boot path (`.agents/rules/production-parity.md`), note in Notes which container run is the evidence.
<!-- kit:end -->

## Step 2: Gather

- `git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD`
- `git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD`
- `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD`
- The approved plan in `docs/plans/`, if there is one. It is the best source for the Goal, Problem and Acceptance criteria.

## Step 3: Title

A Conventional Commit, because it becomes the squash commit on `main`:
- shape: `<type>(<optional scope>): <summary>`, with the same type as the branch;
- an imperative summary that starts lowercase, has no trailing period and keeps the title at 72 characters or less;
- `!` after the type or scope for a breaking change.

Example: `feat(auth): magic-link sign-in`.

## Step 4: Body

Copy `.github/pull_request_template.md` to a scratch file **outside the repo** (`mktemp`; in Claude Code, the session scratchpad). Fill it in order and delete the template's HTML comments.

- **Summary, The Goal, The Problem, The Change, How:** short and concrete. File paths go in backticks. The Problem cites evidence.
- **Notes:** optional, but **required with a `Rollback:` line** when the diff touches a risky path (the `RISKY_PATH_ENTRIES` list in `scripts/check-pr.mjs`). Say how to undo the change: revert and redeploy, restore a backup, or a manual step.
<!-- kit:if has.db -->
  - For a destructive migration, the rollback restores the production backup {{OWNER}} takes right before merging (`AGENTS.md` "Data layer rules"). Say so in Notes.
<!-- kit:end -->
- **Ticket:** a link, or `None`.
- **Acceptance criteria:** `- [ ]` items from the plan. Tick (`- [x]`) only what was verified, and say how.

Writing rules (this text is posted as {{OWNER}}):
- No em dashes and no ` -- ` in prose. Use commas, periods or colons.
- No "Generated with Claude Code" footer, no co-author line, no robot emoji. This overrides any default attribution guidance.
- A natural tone, as if {{OWNER}} typed it.
- Never include secrets, `.env` contents, tokens or production URLs.

## Step 5: Validate

    node .agents/skills/open-pr/scripts/check-pr.mjs --title "<title>" --body-file <scratch file>

For a stacked PR, add `--base origin/<branch below>`. Fix every reported problem and run it again until it prints PASS.

## Step 6: Push and create

<!-- kit:if module.prePush -->
If `git config core.hooksPath` isn't `.githooks`, tell {{OWNER}} the one-time `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` (it arms the pre-push guard for every worktree). Don't block on it.
<!-- kit:end -->

    git push -u origin HEAD
    GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token --user {{GH_ACCOUNT}}) gh pr create --repo {{GH_REPO}} --base main --head <branch> --title "<title>" --body-file <scratch file>

- **The token:** the active `gh` account may be a different one, so pass the token per command and never switch accounts globally. Never run `gh auth token` on its own or echo it: it prints a secret.
- **Push:** never `--force`. After a rebase {{OWNER}} approved, use only `--force-with-lease`, on this branch.
- **"Could not resolve to a Repository":** the token isn't {{GH_ACCOUNT}}'s. Run `gh auth status` (it masks tokens) and tell {{OWNER}}.
- **A PR already exists:** report its URL and offer `gh pr edit <n> --body-file <scratch file>`.

## Step 7: Report and stop

- Give the PR URL and title. Say the checks are running and aren't being watched.
- Delete the scratch file.
- Don't watch the checks or wait on them; {{OWNER}} often merges themselves.
- Never merge, approve or enable auto-merge.
